gazL(){return'Every row on this card is an amount of money, not a return percentage.\n\nThe "You" row is your profit: what you hold today, plus the cash you got back from sells and dividends, minus everything you put in.\n\nThis is a different figure from the "Return on cost" percentage on the "Real vs Paper" card. Return on cost (Real vs Paper) \u2192 counts dividends and realised gains as profit too, and divides by the cost of the shares they were earned on, held and sold. For a yearly rate that accounts for when you invested, see the Personal IRR card.\n\nEvery target on the leaderboard is measured the same way \u2014 including its own dividends, counted as cash exactly like yours \u2014 so the comparison is fair.'},
