gaOe(){return'Log the money you add to (deposit) or take out of (withdrawal) your account. The running total becomes your available cash balance.\n\nWhat your cash affects: it counts toward your Total wealth and your concentration % on the Analysis tab (it shows as a "Cash" slice in the diversification donut), and nothing else. It does NOT change your returns (IRR), risk metrics (VaR, Sharpe, beta) or the equity curve \u2014 those are based on your holdings only.\n\nBuying a stock does not automatically reduce this balance yet \u2014 if you invest your cash, log a withdrawal so the number stays accurate.\n\nOptionally attach a flow to one portfolio (tag). Your available balance never goes below zero, though the history keeps the true deposits and withdrawals.'},
